-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- cold-emailing
DO $academy$
DECLARE pid uuid; can_write boolean;
BEGIN
  SELECT id, (content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review' OR version < 2) INTO pid, can_write FROM academy_programs WHERE slug = 'cold-emailing';
  IF pid IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-emailing not found — run academy-migration-standalone.sql first'; RETURN; END IF;
  IF NOT can_write THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-emailing content already approved — left unchanged'; RETURN; END IF;
  UPDATE academy_programs SET version = 2, content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review', learning_objectives = ARRAY[$o$Write a cold email with one specific observation and one clear ask.$o$, $o$Keep emails short, honest and easy to answer.$o$, $o$Follow up without pressure and stop when asked.$o$, $o$Use only owner-approved templates for anything with claims.$o$]::text[],
    practical_prompt = NULL, practical_rubric = '[]'::jsonb WHERE id = pid;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 1, $t$The Anatomy of a Cold Email That Gets Read$t$, ARRAY[$o$Write a subject line and opening that earn a read.$o$, $o$Keep to one clear ask.$o$]::text[], $b$A cold email has seconds to earn a second look. The structure that works, and that Nova teaches:
1. SUBJECT — short, specific, honest. A real observation beats a trick. "Two phone numbers on your listing" is better than "Quick question!!!".
2. LINE ONE — the one real observation you made, and where.
3. LINE TWO — connect it to a possible cost in plain words, without a number: "Customers might not know which one to call."
4. ONE ASK — a short call, or a reply with a good time. Not three asks.
5. SIGN-OFF — your name, Nova Systems, and a simple way to say no.

Keep it under about 120 words. If you cannot find a real specific to mention, the email is not ready — go back to prospecting.

EXAMPLE (fictional):
Subject: Two phone numbers on your listing
"Hi Dana — I noticed the Google listing for Riverside Auto shows 203-555-0100 and your website shows 203-555-0199. Customers may not know which one reaches you. I look at how local businesses handle new inquiries and write down what I find. Would a 15-minute call this week be useful? If it isn't, just tell me and I won't follow up. — Sam, Nova Systems"

NEVER SAY in a cold email: guarantees, invented figures, claims about other clients, or "free" offers you have not been approved to make.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 2, $t$Personalisation Without Fabrication$t$, ARRAY[$o$Personalise using verified facts only.$o$, $o$Avoid fake familiarity and merge-tag mistakes.$o$]::text[], $b$Personalisation means referring to something true and specific about their business. It does not mean flattering them, pretending to know them, or inventing a detail.

Rules:
• Only mention what you verified. If you are not sure the detail is current, say "your website currently shows…".
• Do not claim you "recently used" their service or "know a customer of theirs" unless it is true.
• Merge-fields can embarrass you: read every email in full before sending; never send a template with brackets still in it.
• Do not use the recipient's personal social media, family or private details.

TEST: could a stranger reading your first line tell you looked at THIS business? If the line would fit any business, it is not personalisation.

EXERCISE IDEA: take a template and replace every generic phrase with a specific fact. If you cannot replace a phrase with a fact, delete the phrase.

WHEN YOU HAVE NOTHING SPECIFIC: send nothing. A short, honest referral request or a visit is better than a fabricated compliment.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 3, $t$Follow-Up Without Being Pushy$t$, ARRAY[$o$Plan a respectful follow-up cadence.$o$, $o$Add value or clarity, not pressure.$o$, $o$Stop when asked or when the sequence ends.$o$]::text[], $b$Most replies come after a follow-up, and most annoyance comes from bad follow-ups. A respectful cadence: a first email; one follow-up two or three business days later; one more about a week after that; then stop, with a polite closing note if you like. Three touches, then rest.

Each follow-up should add something: a clearer question, a second observation, or an easier way to reply ("Reply 'yes' and I'll send two times"). "Just checking in" adds nothing.

SCRIPT — second touch: "Hi Dana — following up on the two phone numbers on your listing. If it's already sorted, no need to reply. If it's useful to talk for 15 minutes, tell me a time that suits you."

SCRIPT — closing note: "I'll stop here so I don't clutter your inbox. If handling new inquiries ever becomes a priority, I'm happy to look at it with you."

IF SOMEONE SAYS STOP or "unsubscribe": stop at once, mark the contact do-not-contact, and do not send anything else. Log the follow-ups you send so your manager can see the cadence.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 4, $t$Deliverability, Honesty and the Rules of the Road$t$, ARRAY[$o$Avoid practices that harm deliverability and trust.$o$, $o$Include honest sender identification.$o$, $o$Respect opt-out requests.$o$]::text[], $b$Sending email is a privilege you can lose. Simple practices:
• Send from your real Nova identity; say who you are and what Nova Systems is.
• Do not use misleading subjects, fake "Re:" or "Fwd:", or pretend an existing relationship.
• Do not attach files in a cold email; a link to nothing suspicious is enough, and only if approved.
• Send at human volumes. Your manager will tell you the sensible daily limit; do not try to beat it.
• Include an easy way to decline in the text of the email (for example "Reply 'no thanks' and I will not email again.") and honour it immediately.
• Never email a contact marked do-not-contact.

BUSINESS EMAIL vs CONSUMER: cold emails to businesses about business services are handled differently from marketing to consumers, and the rules differ by place. Nova's approved templates in the Sales Toolkit have been reviewed for the basics; use them. If you want to change wording that makes any claim, ask your manager first.

CHECKLIST BEFORE SEND: (1) real specific observation; (2) one ask; (3) no claim, figure or guarantee; (4) opt-out sentence; (5) contact is not do-not-contact; (6) logged as an activity.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 5, $t$Turning a Reply Into a Conversation$t$, ARRAY[$o$Answer replies quickly and honestly.$o$, $o$Move a warm reply to a short call.$o$, $o$Handle "not interested" and "send me info" gracefully.$o$]::text[], $b$A reply is the start, not the finish. Answer the same day if you can. Keep it short, answer the question they asked, and propose one next step.

COMMON REPLIES:
• "Sounds interesting — tell me more." → Do not send a brochure. "Happy to. It's easiest to ask you two quick questions first so I show you something relevant: how do customers usually reach you, and what happens when nobody picks up? Could we speak for 15 minutes on [two times]?"
• "Send me some info." → "Sure — so I send something relevant rather than generic, what's the main thing you'd want to fix or know more about?" (Then follow up with the approved material.)
• "Not interested." → "Thanks for letting me know — I won't follow up. If things change, I'm around." Log it and close.
• "How much is it?" → "The scope decides the price, so I don't want to guess. After a short conversation I can bring a written proposal." (Never quote a price that is not approved.)
• "Take me off your list." → stop, apologise briefly, mark do-not-contact.

BOOKING: offer two specific times, confirm by email, and put the discovery in your pipeline as Discovery Scheduled once it is real.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 1, $q$What makes the best cold-email subject line?$q$, $c$["Short, specific and honest, based on a real observation","A trick like \"Re: our conversation\"","ALL CAPS urgency","A promise of results"]$c$::jsonb, 0, $e$Honest, specific subjects earn reads without misleading anyone.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 2, $q$How many asks should a cold email contain?$q$, $c$["Three, so one lands","As many as fit","None","One clear ask"]$c$::jsonb, 3, $e$One clear ask is easier to answer and to say yes to.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 3, $q$You cannot find anything specific about a business. What do you do?$q$, $c$["Invent a compliment","Do not send an email; go back to prospecting or use a referral or visit","Send a generic template anyway","Copy another rep's email"]$c$::jsonb, 1, $e$If there is no real specific, the email is not ready.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 4, $q$Which line is acceptable in a cold email?$q$, $c$["\"Our clients typically see revenue double.\"","\"I noticed your listing and website show different closing times.\"","\"We guarantee more customers.\"","\"You are definitely losing money.\""]$c$::jsonb, 1, $e$Only verified observations are allowed; results, guarantees and losses are not.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 5, $q$What is a respectful follow-up cadence?$q$, $c$["Daily until they answer","Only one email ever","One email every hour","A first email, a follow-up in 2–3 business days, another about a week later, then stop"]$c$::jsonb, 3, $e$Three touches with added value, then rest.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 6, $q$What should every follow-up do?$q$, $c$["Add something — a clearer question, a second observation or an easier way to reply","Say \"just checking in\"","Threaten to close the offer","Copy the manager"]$c$::jsonb, 0, $e$"Just checking in" adds nothing.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 7, $q$A recipient replies "unsubscribe". What do you do?$q$, $c$["Send one last email","Wait 30 days","Stop immediately, mark do-not-contact, log it","Ask them why"]$c$::jsonb, 2, $e$A request to stop is final and must be recorded.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 8, $q$A prospect replies "How much is it?" and there is no approved price. What is the honest answer?$q$, $c$["Guess a friendly number","\"Around a thousand\"","\"I can't tell you anything.\"","\"The scope decides it, so I won't guess. After a short conversation I can bring a written proposal.\""]$c$::jsonb, 3, $e$No unapproved prices; the proposal carries the price.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 9, $q$Which is a misleading practice?$q$, $c$["Saying who you are and what Nova is","An easy opt-out sentence","A subject line beginning \"Re:\" for an email that is not a reply","Reading every email before sending"]$c$::jsonb, 2, $e$Fake replies mislead the recipient and damage deliverability and trust.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_quiz_questions (program_id, order_index, question, choices, correct_index, explanation, critical) VALUES (pid, 10, $q$A rep changes an approved template to add "we typically save clients thousands." What is wrong?$q$, $c$["It adds an unapproved claim and an invented figure; wording with claims needs owner approval","Nothing","It is too short","It is too personal"]$c$::jsonb, 0, $e$Invented figures and unapproved claims are forbidden.$e$, false)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET question = EXCLUDED.question, choices = EXCLUDED.choices, correct_index = EXCLUDED.correct_index, explanation = EXCLUDED.explanation, critical = EXCLUDED.critical;
  INSERT INTO academy_exercises (program_id, order_index, lesson_order, title, prompt, self_check, model_answer) VALUES (pid, 1, 1, $t$Draft a four-line cold email$t$, $p$Using the structure from the lesson, draft a cold email of four to six short lines for a real, public local business (do not send it). Include an honest opt-out sentence.$p$, $s$["Is line one a real, verifiable observation?","Is there exactly one ask?","Is there any figure, guarantee or claim? (There should be none.)","Is there an easy way to say no?"]$s$::jsonb, $m$Subject: Two closing times on your listing
Hi Dana — the Google listing for Riverside Auto shows a 5 pm close; your website says 6 pm. Customers may not know which is right. I look at how local businesses handle new inquiries and write down what I find. Could we talk for 15 minutes this week? If not, reply "no thanks" and I won't email again. — Sam, Nova Systems$m$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET lesson_order = EXCLUDED.lesson_order, title = EXCLUDED.title, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, self_check = EXCLUDED.self_check, model_answer = EXCLUDED.model_answer;
  INSERT INTO academy_exercises (program_id, order_index, lesson_order, title, prompt, self_check, model_answer) VALUES (pid, 2, 3, $t$Write the second touch$t$, $p$You emailed a prospect four days ago and heard nothing. Write the follow-up that adds something and is easy to answer.$p$, $s$["Does it add a clearer question or second observation?","Does it avoid \"just checking in\" and pressure?","Is there an easy, low-effort way to reply?"]$s$::jsonb, $m$Hi Dana — following up on the closing times. One more thing I noticed: the phone number on the site goes to voicemail after 5 pm. Is that intentional? If it would help to talk for 15 minutes, tell me a time that suits you; if it's all sorted, no need to reply.$m$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET lesson_order = EXCLUDED.lesson_order, title = EXCLUDED.title, prompt = EXCLUDED.prompt, self_check = EXCLUDED.self_check, model_answer = EXCLUDED.model_answer;
END
$academy$;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- cold-calling
DO $academy$
DECLARE pid uuid; can_write boolean;
BEGIN
  SELECT id, (content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review' OR version < 2) INTO pid, can_write FROM academy_programs WHERE slug = 'cold-calling';
  IF pid IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-calling not found — run academy-migration-standalone.sql first'; RETURN; END IF;
  IF NOT can_write THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-calling content already approved — left unchanged'; RETURN; END IF;
  UPDATE academy_programs SET version = 2, content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review', learning_objectives = ARRAY[$o$Open a call in a way that earns the next ten seconds honestly.$o$, $o$Handle the gatekeeper and the voicemail respectfully.$o$, $o$Handle objections without pressure or invented claims.$o$, $o$Book a discovery conversation and log the call correctly.$o$]::text[],
    practical_prompt = NULL, practical_rubric = '[]'::jsonb WHERE id = pid;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 1, $t$The First Ten Seconds$t$, ARRAY[$o$Identify yourself and the reason for the call plainly.$o$, $o$Ask permission and earn a minute.$o$]::text[], $b$A cold call interrupts someone. The respectful way to start is to say so. A structure that works:
1. Your name and company: "Hi, this is Sam from Nova Systems."
2. Honest reason in one sentence: "I look at how local businesses handle new customer inquiries."
3. Permission: "Did I catch you at a bad time?" or "Do you have a minute for a quick question?"
4. Your one specific reason for calling THEM (the observation you noted).

EXAMPLE (fictional): "Hi, this is Sam from Nova Systems. I look at how local businesses handle new customer inquiries. I noticed your listing shows two phone numbers and wanted to ask which one customers should use. Do you have a minute?"

What to avoid: pretending you are returning their call, using a false name, rushing to a pitch, or reading a script in a flat voice. People forgive an honest interruption; they do not forgive a trick.

IF THEY SAY "I'm busy": "Understood — when would be a better time for two minutes?" Write down the time and call then. If they say not to call again, thank them, stop, and mark do-not-contact.

BEFORE YOU DIAL: have your observation written in front of you, your CRM lead open, and a pen. Do not dial without a reason for THIS business.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 2, $t$Gatekeepers, Voicemail and Callbacks$t$, ARRAY[$o$Treat gatekeepers as colleagues, not obstacles.$o$, $o$Leave a short, honest voicemail.$o$, $o$Schedule callbacks and keep them.$o$]::text[], $b$The person who answers the phone at a small business is often the very person the diagnostic is about: they may be the one who is overwhelmed. Treat them with respect and be truthful.

GATEKEEPER: "Hi, I'm Sam from Nova Systems. Could you tell me who looks after how new customer inquiries are handled — is that the owner or someone else?" Ask for a name and the best time to reach them. Never lie about who you are or what the call is about. If they will take a message, leave a short one and note their name.

VOICEMAIL (under 25 seconds): "Hi [name], this is Sam from Nova Systems, 203-555-0100 (use your real number). I look at how local businesses handle new inquiries and noticed something on your listing I wanted to ask about. I'll try you again on Thursday morning; if you'd rather I didn't, just say so and I won't." Do not leave figures or promises.

CALLBACKS: when someone asks you to call back at a time, put it in the system as a dated next action immediately, and call at that time. A kept callback is the most credible thing you can do.

LIMITS: do not call the same number repeatedly in a day; follow your manager's cadence guidance; and never call outside reasonable business hours. Log every attempt, including no-answer and voicemail, with an outcome.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 3, $t$Handling Objections Honestly$t$, ARRAY[$o$Understand what an objection is really asking.$o$, $o$Respond with a question and evidence, not pressure.$o$, $o$Accept a genuine no.$o$]::text[], $b$An objection is usually a question or a worry in disguise. The pattern: acknowledge, ask, respond honestly, offer a small next step — or accept the no.

• "We're not interested." → "That's fair. Can I ask what's working well for you with new customers at the moment? I ask because I only reach out when I notice something specific, and I may have got it wrong." If they still decline, thank them and end.
• "We already have a website/agency." → "Good. Nova doesn't replace that. We look at how inquiries are actually handled and write down what we find; sometimes the answer is 'you're fine'. Would that be useful as a second opinion?"
• "Send me an email." → "Happy to. So I send you something relevant rather than generic, what's the one thing you'd most want to know?" Then send only approved material.
• "How much does it cost?" → "The scope decides it, so I won't guess. After a short conversation I can bring a written proposal." NEVER SAY a made-up number.
• "Does it work?" → "I can't promise a result. What I can do is show you what's actually happening today, with evidence, so you can decide."
• "I don't have time." → "I understand. Would ten minutes on Thursday be easier?"

If the answer is a firm no, thank them. A respectful no today is a future yes. If they say do not call again: stop and mark do-not-contact.

NEVER: argue, invent urgency ("this offer ends today"), guarantee results, or disparage a competitor.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 4, $t$Booking the Discovery Conversation$t$, ARRAY[$o$Ask for a specific, small next step.$o$, $o$Confirm the time and who will attend.$o$, $o$Record it correctly so it counts.$o$]::text[], $b$The purpose of a cold call is not to sell. It is to book a conversation where you can ask about the business properly. The ask: "Would it be useful to talk for 20 minutes on Tuesday at 10 or Wednesday at 2, so I can ask a few questions about how inquiries reach you?"

Give two specific times. Confirm the person's name and role, whether the decision maker will be there, and how to reach them (phone, video, or visit). Read it back.

AFTER THE CALL, in the system: (1) log the call with what happened, honestly; (2) set the contact details; (3) move to Qualified only when your qualification note is real; (4) move to Discovery Scheduled with the actual future date and time — the system requires a future time and a named contact; (5) set a next action to send a confirmation.

CONFIRMATION MESSAGE (approved in the Toolkit): "Hi Dana — confirming our conversation Tuesday at 10 about how new inquiries reach Riverside Auto. I'll bring a few questions; there's nothing to prepare. Reply if you need to move it."

NO-SHOWS: send one polite message offering two new times; do not chase more than twice.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 5, $t$Logging Calls and Improving$t$, ARRAY[$o$Log every call factually.$o$, $o$Review your own calls weekly.$o$, $o$Learn from outcomes without inflating them.$o$]::text[], $b$Every call gets a log entry: what happened, the outcome (no answer, left message, spoke with contact, meeting booked, not interested, wrong number), and the next action. "Spoke with owner, asked to call back Thursday 10" is useful; "good call" is not.

Be honest in outcomes. Logging "meeting booked" when someone said "maybe" harms you: your manager plans around your pipeline and the system's stage rules will not let you skip steps.

WEEKLY REVIEW (15 minutes): count your attempts, connects and booked conversations from the log. Pick one call that went badly and write what you would say differently. Pick one that went well and write why. Share one learning with your manager.

WHAT NOT TO TRACK OR SHARE: never record a caller's sensitive personal information, and never record a call unless you have clear permission and your manager has confirmed the rules for your location. Recording rules vary by place; do not record unless Nova tells you it is allowed.

SCRIPT to yourself before every call: (1) Do I have a specific, true reason to call this business? (2) Is this person allowed to be contacted? (3) Am I ready to accept a no?$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
