$academy$;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- cold-messaging
DO $academy$
DECLARE pid uuid; can_write boolean;
BEGIN
  SELECT id, (content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review' OR version < 2) INTO pid, can_write FROM academy_programs WHERE slug = 'cold-messaging';
  IF pid IS NULL THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-messaging not found — run academy-migration-standalone.sql first'; RETURN; END IF;
  IF NOT can_write THEN RAISE NOTICE 'program cold-messaging content already approved — left unchanged'; RETURN; END IF;
  UPDATE academy_programs SET version = 2, content_review_status = 'pending_owner_review', learning_objectives = ARRAY[$o$Choose the right channel and etiquette for social, direct-message and text outreach.$o$, $o$Respect consent, especially for text messages.$o$, $o$Write short, honest messages that invite a reply.$o$, $o$Move a reply toward a booked conversation and keep records.$o$]::text[],
    practical_prompt = NULL, practical_rubric = '[]'::jsonb WHERE id = pid;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 1, $t$Channels and Etiquette$t$, ARRAY[$o$Match channel to context.$o$, $o$Follow each channel's norms and Nova's rules.$o$]::text[], $b$Messaging feels casual but it is still an interruption, and each channel has rules.

• BUSINESS ACCOUNTS ON SOCIAL PLATFORMS: a short, professional message to the business page inbox is normal. Do not message personal profiles about business unless there is a real connection.
• EMAIL: covered in Program 3.
• TEXT MESSAGES (SMS): texting a person's number needs their recorded consent first. A cold text to a number you found is not allowed unless your manager confirms the consent basis. When in doubt, do not text — call or email instead.
• MESSAGING APPS: same rule as text — do not message unknown numbers.

GENERAL ETIQUETTE: use your real name and Nova Systems; one short message, not a stream; no links you do not control; no attachments; no emojis that make you look like a bot; do not message late at night; never send the same text to lists.

REMEMBER: every message must be honest and provable, contain no figures or guarantees, and never go to a do-not-contact person.

CHECKLIST: (1) Is this channel appropriate for this person? (2) Do I have consent if it is a text? (3) Is my message short, honest and specific? (4) Will I log it?$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 2, $t$Consent for Text Messages$t$, ARRAY[$o$Explain what valid consent is.$o$, $o$Never text without it.$o$, $o$Honour opt-outs instantly.$o$]::text[], $b$Text-message consent is stricter than for email or phone, and mistakes are costly to the business and to the recipient. The safe rule at Nova: you only text someone who has given their own recorded permission to be texted by Nova, for the purpose they agreed to.

WHAT COUNTS: the person ticked a clear, unbundled consent box or told you clearly that texting is fine and it was recorded by the system with the date and source. WHAT DOES NOT: they gave you their number; you imported a list; a colleague said it was fine; they did not object.

YOU CANNOT MARK CONSENT: only the person themselves, through Nova's consent capture, creates it. If you edit a contact, consent flags do not change.

EVERY TEXT must identify Nova Systems and include a simple way to stop ("Reply STOP to opt out"). If someone replies STOP (or any clear request to stop), stop immediately — the opt-out applies to all further texts.

APPROVED TEXT (example): "Hi Dana, this is Sam from Nova Systems, following up on our call. Would Tuesday 10am still work? Reply STOP to opt out."

WHEN NO CONSENT EXISTS: call or email instead, or ask on the phone: "Is it okay if I text you a confirmation?" and let the consent be recorded properly.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 3, $t$Writing Messages People Answer$t$, ARRAY[$o$Write short, specific messages.$o$, $o$Use one question or one ask.$o$, $o$Avoid pressure and hype.$o$]::text[], $b$A good message is two to four short lines: who you are, one specific true observation, one easy question.

EXAMPLE — business page DM (fictional): "Hi — Sam from Nova Systems. I noticed your booking page shows Saturday hours your Google listing doesn't. Which is right? I look at how local businesses handle new inquiries and thought it might be worth flagging."

EXAMPLE — reply to a "who is this?": "Sam from Nova Systems — I look at how local businesses handle new customer inquiries. Sorry for the surprise; I noticed the hours mismatch and thought I'd flag it. Happy to leave it there if you'd rather."

DO: ask one question; be specific; give them an easy out. DON'T: send a wall of text; use hype ("game-changer!"); send follow-ups within hours; send a link and nothing else; or claim you have "helped businesses like yours" unless there is an approved case study you may cite.

FOLLOW-UP: one gentle follow-up after 2–3 days; a final short closing note after about a week; then stop.

READ IT ALOUD: if it sounds like a robot or a salesperson wrote it, rewrite it as if messaging a busy neighbour.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 4, $t$From Reply to Booked Conversation$t$, ARRAY[$o$Answer promptly and honestly.$o$, $o$Move to a call or visit.$o$, $o$Keep records of every exchange.$o$]::text[], $b$When someone replies, answer quickly and keep it human. Suggested flow: thank them; answer their question honestly; suggest a short call or visit; offer two times; confirm by their preferred channel.

EXAMPLES:
• They ask "What is this about?" → "Nova looks at how local businesses handle new inquiries and writes down what it finds. I noticed a mismatch in your listing and wanted to ask about it — could we talk for 15 minutes? I can do Tuesday 10 or Wednesday 2."
• They ask price → "The scope decides it, so I won't guess. After a short conversation I can bring a written proposal."
• They say "not now" → "No problem — I'll check back in a few weeks unless you'd rather I didn't." Set a dated next action.
• They say stop → stop, mark do-not-contact.

MOVE OFF TEXT: once interest is real, move to a call or meeting; important details belong in a proper conversation, not a text thread.

RECORDING: log each message you send and each reply, with the channel and outcome. Do not screenshot private conversations to share outside Nova. Record what matters in the CRM in your own words.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
  INSERT INTO academy_lessons (program_id, order_index, title, objectives, body) VALUES (pid, 5, $t$Protecting Yourself and the Prospect$t$, ARRAY[$o$Recognise risky requests.$o$, $o$Avoid scams and impersonation.$o$, $o$Escalate concerns.$o$]::text[], $b$Messaging channels attract scams and impersonators, and you represent Nova. Protect yourself and prospects:
• Never ask for or accept payment, passwords, codes, identity documents or bank details in a message. Payment happens only on the payment provider's hosted page from an official Nova proposal.
• Do not click links from unknown senders; do not share your Nova login; do not use personal accounts to represent Nova unless your manager says so.
• If someone claims to be from Nova asking you to do something unusual (send money, change a payout account), it is not Nova. Tell your manager.
• If a prospect seems distressed, confused, or vulnerable, slow down, be kind, and involve your manager. Do not press a sale.
• Do not discuss other clients or their results.

ESCALATE (tell your manager) when: someone threatens legal action, alleges harassment, asks you to delete records, or you are unsure whether contacting them is allowed. Escalating early is professional.

SELF-CHECK: "Would I be comfortable if Nova's owner read this thread?" If not, stop and ask.$b$)
    ON CONFLICT (program_id, order_index) DO UPDATE SET title = EXCLUDED.title, objectives = EXCLUDED.objectives, body = EXCLUDED.body;
